Z||000009||Gerald||10-01-2001||10:11 PM||||Well Ive been hearing rumers in the GM world that the Opel Speedster might be coming to north america as a pontiac model. And it would be the perfect car in my opion to carry the fiero name.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||10-01-2001||11:19 PM||||As long as the Corvette exists, GM will not let the Fiero become what I know it could have been.  Having said that, I don't want it to come back given the constraints it would have.  I would welcome a new Fiero.  The design is open in many regards, but it <B><I>MUST</B></I> be a mid engined 2 seater.  Period.  It would be great for a new Fiero to replace the Firebird, but again, you've got the 'Vette competition to worry about.  Still, the Fiero's we (the Pennock's community) have been building for the last several years show just how sound the platform can be with modern technology.  Pontiac could build an inexpensive world beater, if only they'd be allowed to.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rick 88||10-01-2001||11:33 PM||||It would depend on how it was built.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My new Fiero would be built on a platform similar to the current car using the plastic body panels. It would have all the current safety equipment plus larger vented discs with ABS, and all speed selectable traction control. The 88 electric power steering would finally be made available. A limited slip version the the current GM Getrag 5-speed transaxle would be standard on the GT. The base car would use the twin cam four from the Saturn L series. Drive one and you will know why I picked this engine. Great torque off the line and 140 hp.<P>The GT would use the 215 horse 24 valve 4 cam Olds "Shortstar" V6. For the true enthusiast a GTR "Ram Air" version would have a supercharged, aftercooled version of the V6 developing 300 rear wheel horsepower.<P>Instead of T-Top's a removable Targa top would be an option, as would a 500 watt "Monsoon" CD/MP3/Satellite radio system. Base cars would get 16in. wheels, GT's 17's, and GTR's would get 18's on the rear.<P>No, I'm not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> just building my dream Fiero out loud. LMK what you think!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rick 88<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000012||Sage||10-01-2001||11:43 PM||||Rick;<P>Please let me know when you will be taking orders for the GTR version.  Black or yellow will be all right.<P>Thanks<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000013||NOS3800||10-01-2001||11:44 PM||||I think the Opel speedster would do the Fiero justice, but from what I understand, it would be badged as a Saturn. Looks like Pontiac is going into the Sport Wagon and sporty sport ute market. ex. VIBE. I feel Pontiac has lost its touch. Its not "exciting" anymore. All of GM has lost touch. Look at the potential. They have a supercharged GrandAm, but it will probably never make production. Why? The Monte Carlo SS has the NA3800. Shouldn't it have the SC 3800? No manual trnnies on any of the V6 powered cars( Grand AM, GP, GA, Alero, etc.) The Quad Four keeps getting revised, but each time it looses 10 HP. Its now called the Ecotec, makes 140HP. It will be in the Cavs and Sunfires in a market against 170 HP Focus SVT, 160 HP Civic Si, 150 HP NEON( SC version coming soon). <BR>In a perfect world, they would make a all new Fiero on a chassis shared with the Saturn Sport Coupe. Or maybe a all new chassis. I mean if Mazda can make a low volume MR2 Spyder, why not GM? Power choices would be the Ecotech for the base model( gotta be realistic) and for the topline model, a SC3800 mated to a manual 6 speed! You could offer a mid level car with the NA 3800 or 3400 6's. It would be a convertable, with a hardtop stripped down boyracer a year later! Car should weigh around 2200-2500 pounds max! Anyway, I need to stop dreaming....<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@101.12 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BillCar2001_4.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000014||Rick 88||10-02-2001||12:10 AM||||Sage,<P>I'll have your order sheet ready soon!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously, I was a Sales Manager for a Pontiac dealership for many years. I used to build dealership "Tuner" versions of Sunfires', Grand Ams', and Firebirds' for local customers. We also sold Firehawks', Mecham Trans Ams' and Mecham Grand Prixs'. The dealerships nickname for my Tuner cars were "Ricky Racers".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sage:<BR><B>Rick;<P>Please let me know when you will be taking orders for the GTR version.  Black or yellow will be all right.<P>Thanks<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||10
Z||000015||Fformula88||10-02-2001||10:45 AM||||Bringing up the Mazda Miata and MR2 Spyder is a great example here.  Remember the Fiero convertible prototypes Pontiac was showing in the 80's?  The Fiero goes out of production in the summer of 88 not long after, Mazda starts the roadster revolution with the Miata!  Maybe Pontiac had the key to selling Fiero's righ under their noses and didn't even know it!<P>Next Fiero needs a roadster version!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Rick 88||10-02-2001||05:55 PM||||Just how have Aztek sales compared to Fiero's? Since the Fiero is impractical the Aztek should have trashed it in sales. I bet thats not the case. <P>Maybe now that Robert Lutz (a real car guy)is working for GM instead of Chrysler, they might actually build some nice looking cars again. It may be a good time to campaign for a new Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rick 88||||reg||4
